WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.741
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:13.096 --> 00:14.556
[bird screeching]

4
00:37.287 --> 00:40.666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

5
00:52.386 --> 00:53.470
[gasps]

6
00:54.846 --> 00:57.015
[♪ tense music playing]

7
01:16.118 --> 01:18.453
Get your hands off of her!

8
01:18.537 --> 01:19.913
[gasps]

9
01:19.997 --> 01:21.415
[both grunting]

10
01:27.838 --> 01:29.756
You bastard!

11
01:33.802 --> 01:35.095
[Navier] Brother!

12
01:38.348 --> 01:39.433
What? "Brother"?

13
01:39.516 --> 01:42.561
Yes, I am her brother, you swine!

14
01:42.644 --> 01:44.896
Ah, Kosair, what on earth are you doing?

15
01:46.023 --> 01:47.024
Who is this punk?

16
01:47.107 --> 01:49.026
He's Prince Heinrey of the Western Kingdom.

17
01:49.109 --> 01:50.736
How dare he embrace you, huh?

18
01:52.195 --> 01:53.363
He's a friend.

19
01:53.447 --> 01:55.991
Friend or not, the only ones who can embrace you

20
01:56.074 --> 01:58.201
is me and that son of a bitch, Sovieshu.

21
01:59.077 --> 02:00.245
Please leave right now.

22
02:00.329 --> 02:01.997
[Navier panting]

23
02:10.422 --> 02:11.673
[door opens]

24
02:11.757 --> 02:13.008
-Ah. -Ah.

25
02:14.801 --> 02:15.802
[sighs]

26
02:16.595 --> 02:17.596
My sister.

27
02:17.679 --> 02:19.348
[sighs] Brother.

28
02:24.269 --> 02:25.729
[exclaims]

29
02:25.812 --> 02:27.272
[panting softly]

30
02:32.319 --> 02:33.403
[whispers] Go on.

31
02:40.035 --> 02:42.621
[straining] Kosair, I'm really happy to see you too,

32
02:43.288 --> 02:44.956
but you're squeezing too tight.

33
02:45.040 --> 02:46.166
Oh, right. Yes.

34
02:46.249 --> 02:48.043
-Ah, sorry. -[exhales]

35
02:51.838 --> 02:52.881
You've lost weight.

36
02:54.216 --> 02:55.217
I have not, Kosair.

37
02:55.300 --> 02:56.510
Oh, no.

38
02:56.593 --> 02:58.929
You're skin and bones. You just don't see it.

39
02:59.012 --> 03:00.472
No, I am not.

40
03:01.056 --> 03:02.057
You just don't see it.

41
03:05.727 --> 03:07.354
Anyway, that bastard.

42
03:08.230 --> 03:10.232
How dare he even look at somebody else?

43
03:11.775 --> 03:13.110
Ah, so…

44
03:13.193 --> 03:15.028
The box here, is it for me?

45
03:15.112 --> 03:16.279
I'll open it.

46
03:18.490 --> 03:20.200
Will you stop scowling?

47
03:22.911 --> 03:24.162
Ah!

48
03:29.376 --> 03:31.169
Uh, so… what do you think?

49
03:31.253 --> 03:33.130
Uh… Oh, it's…

50
03:36.007 --> 03:37.008
Uh…

51
03:37.759 --> 03:38.844
It's very…

52
03:43.765 --> 03:44.891
It's very pretty.

53
03:46.059 --> 03:48.311
[laughs] Yes! I knew it!

54
03:51.606 --> 03:52.607
[sighs]

55
03:55.652 --> 03:57.863
The Empress must be in great distress right now.

56
03:58.613 --> 03:59.948
[Heinrey] Hmm.

57
04:00.031 --> 04:02.742
Although her brother did just try to kill me.

58
04:02.826 --> 04:04.619
Why would… Wait. Hold on a minute.

59
04:05.120 --> 04:07.205
-Are you saying that her brother is here? -Hmm.

60
04:07.289 --> 04:09.916
Her Majesty's brother, General Kosair? That one?

61
04:10.959 --> 04:13.044
The same general who's undefeated?

62
04:13.879 --> 04:15.172
He's won every fight, you know.

63
04:16.131 --> 04:17.924
I just said I was almost killed.

64
04:18.008 --> 04:19.384
You're alive, so it's fine.

65
04:19.468 --> 04:21.344
So, tell me, when did he get here? Why did he come here?

66
04:21.428 --> 04:22.429
What is he doing here?

67
04:22.512 --> 04:23.889
Oh, uh, what?

68
04:23.972 --> 04:25.432
When is he leaving? Huh?

69
04:25.515 --> 04:27.684
I just told you I was nearly skewered! He was…

70
04:27.768 --> 04:29.352
[imitates sword swishing] …swinging it like this.

71
04:29.436 --> 04:31.772
If I hadn't dodged it, the sword would have…

72
04:31.855 --> 04:33.023
[grunts] I almost died!

73
04:33.106 --> 04:34.399
Yes, I see. Good.

74
04:34.483 --> 04:36.443
If I go this way, he's just over there? [squeals]

75
04:36.526 --> 04:37.903
Wait! Are you crazy?

76
04:37.986 --> 04:39.529
If you go now, he'll kill you.

77
04:39.613 --> 04:41.239
I don't care if I die if it's him that kills me.

78
04:41.323 --> 04:42.324
-No. -I have to see!

79
04:43.074 --> 04:44.326
What can I do for you?

80
04:44.409 --> 04:46.036
You came here for me.

81
04:46.119 --> 04:47.287
That is all you can do.

82
04:48.914 --> 04:49.956
So, that girl…

83
04:51.166 --> 04:52.834
She's even expecting his brat?

84
04:52.918 --> 04:54.377
[sighs] Brother…

85
04:54.461 --> 04:55.545
The walls have ears.

86
04:55.629 --> 04:56.630
Watch what you say.

87
04:57.589 --> 04:59.132
That's not how I act.

88
04:59.674 --> 05:01.009
Well, then…

89
05:01.092 --> 05:03.220
I suppose I should kill the two of them right now!

90
05:03.303 --> 05:04.346
[sighs] Stop this, please.

91
05:04.429 --> 05:06.723
You'll be sentenced to death. Don't be a fool.

92
05:06.807 --> 05:08.099
You cannot threaten the Emperor.

93
05:12.270 --> 05:13.688
I should have come sooner.

94
05:17.317 --> 05:19.820
How lonely it must have been all by yourself.

95
05:22.697 --> 05:24.241
I cannot remain Empress…

96
05:25.116 --> 05:26.868
if I cannot endure this.

97
05:27.744 --> 05:28.745
Okay.

98
05:33.959 --> 05:36.044
[♪ majestic music playing]

99
05:36.127 --> 05:38.797
Your Majesty Navier, Empress of the Eastern Empire,

100
05:38.880 --> 05:42.300
Kosair, Commander of the North, humbly reports his return.

101
05:45.053 --> 05:48.640
By Your Majesty's command, I have defeated the Springwater Bandits,

102
05:48.723 --> 05:51.351
established a village for the enemies who surrendered,

103
05:51.434 --> 05:54.020
and I have done all I could to guarantee peace.

104
05:55.021 --> 05:56.815
You have guarded our empire.

105
05:56.898 --> 05:59.568
Your hard work has helped our citizens thrive.

106
06:00.485 --> 06:03.113
The New Year's Ceremony was a success, thanks to you.

107
06:09.786 --> 06:11.162
Your empire is proud.

108
06:11.246 --> 06:13.290
I know Sovieshu is grateful.

109
06:14.457 --> 06:16.418
He will award you the highest honor.

110
06:20.714 --> 06:21.715
[door opens]

111
06:38.648 --> 06:41.234
I, Kosair, Commander of the North,

112
06:41.318 --> 06:42.903
offer greetings upon my return.

113
06:47.574 --> 06:48.992
So you've returned in good health?

114
06:49.868 --> 06:51.328
[spits] I'm pleased.

115
06:55.999 --> 06:58.627
I hear that there have been no further threats.

116
06:58.710 --> 07:01.713
Your Majesty has no concerns and is, in fact, flourishing.

117
07:02.297 --> 07:04.966
I think that perhaps I secured the borders too well.

118
07:07.761 --> 07:08.887
[grunts softly]

119
07:17.020 --> 07:19.397
The look in your eyes, the same as always.

120
07:19.481 --> 07:20.482
Ever insolent…

121
07:20.565 --> 07:21.650
General.

122
07:22.233 --> 07:23.318
[Kosair grunts softly]

123
07:25.195 --> 07:26.613
This look in my eyes

124
07:26.696 --> 07:28.657
is the one that had the Springwater Bandits

125
07:28.740 --> 07:30.200
pissing and shitting in fear.

126
07:30.283 --> 07:31.660
[exhales softly]

127
07:31.743 --> 07:33.328
-[clicks] -[Sovieshu] Do you…

128
07:34.537 --> 07:36.164
dare to glare…

129
07:36.915 --> 07:37.916
[Kosair grunts]

130
07:38.583 --> 07:40.877
…at your Emperor, with those eyes?

131
07:41.961 --> 07:43.254
[grunts]

132
07:44.798 --> 07:47.258
Why would I do that, Your Majesty?

133
07:47.759 --> 07:49.177
[grunts]

134
07:49.719 --> 07:52.305
As you know, I swore an oath to Your Majesty

135
07:52.389 --> 07:54.766
that I'd annihilate the Springwater Bandits.

136
07:54.849 --> 07:59.813
And yet, you yourself failed to honor the one oath I asked you to swear.

137
07:59.896 --> 08:00.939
To cherish my sis--

138
08:03.149 --> 08:04.609
Lante!

139
08:04.693 --> 08:06.361
This concludes the medal-award ceremony.

140
08:09.823 --> 08:11.324
[exhales deeply]

141
08:13.326 --> 08:16.329
But there is a banquet with His Majesty…

142
08:16.413 --> 08:17.831
[Kosair sighs exasperatedly]

143
08:18.957 --> 08:20.458
Emperor!

144
08:21.126 --> 08:22.961
May you always succeed.

145
08:23.044 --> 08:24.295
And stay alive.

146
08:32.929 --> 08:34.389
[footsteps receding]

147
08:35.724 --> 08:38.268
That salute is not traditional.

148
08:40.061 --> 08:41.438
-Why, that-- -Ah, no!

149
08:41.521 --> 08:46.109
I think that I may have seen some people salute like that in the North.

150
08:48.194 --> 08:49.779
Get out. Go on, quickly.

151
08:50.363 --> 08:51.573
[sighs]

152
09:10.800 --> 09:13.053
-[door opens] -[footsteps receding]

153
09:13.136 --> 09:14.429
[door closes]

154
09:22.645 --> 09:24.314
[Rashta breathes deeply]

155
09:26.191 --> 09:27.692
[softly] Your Majesty.

156
09:27.776 --> 09:29.903
[breathes deeply]

157
09:29.986 --> 09:31.112
Were you having a nightmare?

158
09:34.491 --> 09:36.576
Lay down, please. Hold Rashta.

159
09:38.036 --> 09:40.205
[breathes deeply]

160
09:50.381 --> 09:52.133
Have you felt the child?

161
09:52.217 --> 09:53.760
Does it move in your womb?

162
09:55.470 --> 09:58.389
You know, the imperial physician said there's a long way before that.

163
09:58.973 --> 10:00.683
When you do eventually feel it move,

164
10:01.518 --> 10:02.769
you will tell me, won't you?

165
10:04.521 --> 10:05.563
Yes.

166
10:06.106 --> 10:08.358
I will tell you straight away, Your Majesty.

167
10:08.441 --> 10:09.442
[Sovieshu] Hmm.

168
10:10.777 --> 10:14.114
I will instruct Anton right away…

169
10:14.948 --> 10:16.574
to write a lullaby.

170
10:18.785 --> 10:22.622
[Sovieshu humming]

171
10:22.705 --> 10:24.916
[both chuckle]

172
10:27.794 --> 10:29.045
This is your first.

173
10:30.505 --> 10:32.715
Your first child. Aren't you afraid?

174
10:38.179 --> 10:40.181
[♪ ominous music playing]

175
10:42.559 --> 10:44.018
[Lotteshu] Your child is alive.

176
10:46.646 --> 10:47.897
-[whimpering] -You don't…

177
10:47.981 --> 10:49.566
believe me, do you?

178
10:51.526 --> 10:52.902
Shall I show you?

179
10:54.362 --> 10:56.156
[Lotteshu laughs]

180
11:03.413 --> 11:04.914
There's no reason to be.

181
11:08.042 --> 11:09.586
Why would I be afraid…

182
11:10.628 --> 11:11.921
with you by my side?

183
11:16.050 --> 11:17.177
[Sovieshu] Rashta.

184
11:18.303 --> 11:19.304
Yes?

185
11:20.013 --> 11:21.598
[Sovieshu] I want to thank you.

186
11:23.474 --> 11:25.810
Thank you for having my child.

187
11:26.728 --> 11:29.147
Anything you desire is yours.

188
11:30.273 --> 11:32.775
Whether it is something you wish to eat,

189
11:32.859 --> 11:35.570
something that you wish to have, anything.

190
11:35.653 --> 11:36.738
Just tell me.

191
11:39.616 --> 11:40.825
Honestly?

192
11:41.326 --> 11:42.535
[Sovieshu] Of course.

193
11:43.494 --> 11:45.413
The mother has to be happy

194
11:45.955 --> 11:48.833
for the child in the womb to be happy also.

195
11:55.048 --> 11:56.257
What's the matter?

196
11:59.177 --> 12:01.054
I'm so content. [sobs softly]

197
12:03.681 --> 12:05.808
I'm crying from happiness. [inhales sharply]

198
12:06.893 --> 12:08.144
[Sovieshu] Hmm.

199
12:24.118 --> 12:25.328
[gasps]

200
12:25.828 --> 12:28.289
Oh, good heavens! [gasps]

201
12:31.542 --> 12:34.087
[gasps] Good heavens!

202
12:34.671 --> 12:39.175
Even Madam Duchess Joubert sent a gift, congratulating us on your pregnancy.

203
12:39.259 --> 12:41.386
Oh, how cute! [chuckles]

204
12:41.970 --> 12:46.015
This ironclad stronghold looks like it is starting to break.

205
12:47.183 --> 12:48.685
[gasps] Good.

206
12:50.019 --> 12:52.146
Hmm. What do you suppose this is?

207
12:52.230 --> 12:53.231
[Albani] What?

208
12:56.985 --> 12:58.194
[Charles] It looks like hair.

209
12:58.278 --> 12:59.904
[Albani] Hair? Well, who's it from?

210
13:01.406 --> 13:04.158
[Philomena] Hmm. There's no separate mark to show who sent it.

211
13:04.742 --> 13:05.743
There's something inside.

212
13:07.870 --> 13:08.871
[Albani] Read it.

213
13:10.206 --> 13:11.833
[Philomena] "This is Ian's hair."

214
13:12.333 --> 13:13.334
[Albani] Ian?

215
13:15.336 --> 13:16.754
"We called your baby 'Ian'…"

216
13:16.838 --> 13:18.214
[♪ ominous music playing]

217
13:23.469 --> 13:24.679
[clears throat]

218
13:26.472 --> 13:28.558
[door opens, then closes]

219
13:29.767 --> 13:32.562
"We called your baby 'Ian,' Rashta.

220
13:33.688 --> 13:35.356
"As you know, he's a boy.

221
13:35.440 --> 13:36.607
"He looks like you.

222
13:37.984 --> 13:40.820
"His brownish hair is exactly like yours."

223
13:43.114 --> 13:44.240
[gasps]

224
13:45.283 --> 13:47.160
[breathing shakily]

225
13:48.995 --> 13:49.996
[box thuds]

226
13:50.079 --> 13:52.081
[♪ music swells]

227
13:58.171 --> 13:59.589
Is this true, Rashta?

228
14:00.423 --> 14:02.633
[breathing raggedly]

229
14:04.802 --> 14:06.220
I asked you a question.

230
14:06.304 --> 14:07.805
[panting]

231
14:15.229 --> 14:16.981
[♪ music fades]

232
14:24.322 --> 14:26.324
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

233
14:27.325 --> 14:28.910
[Lotteshu] Ah!

234
14:28.993 --> 14:32.121
-There he is! Here you are! -Ah, look who it is!

235
14:32.205 --> 14:33.289
There we go.

236
14:34.499 --> 14:36.125
My dear grandson!

237
14:36.626 --> 14:37.752
[grunts]

238
14:38.544 --> 14:41.964
Anyone could tell that it's Rashta's baby. They look exactly alike! Exactly!

239
14:42.048 --> 14:45.009
I'm telling you, Rashta's looks were stamped all over that baby's face.

240
14:45.093 --> 14:46.719
-Goodness. -[Charles] What are we going to do?

241
14:46.803 --> 14:49.806
If we just sit back and do nothing, something terrible is bound to happen.

242
14:49.889 --> 14:50.932
Firstly…

243
14:51.015 --> 14:52.683
Rashta can go to the palace

244
14:52.767 --> 14:54.435
-and offer 500,000 crans. -Ah.

245
14:54.519 --> 14:56.187
Take the promissory note!

246
14:56.270 --> 14:57.647
[groans]

247
14:57.730 --> 14:59.148
Good heavens! Ugh!

248
15:00.108 --> 15:02.401
Can we be certain the baby that Rashta carries

249
15:02.485 --> 15:04.320
is actually the Emperor's child?

250
15:07.740 --> 15:08.825
She played innocent.

251
15:08.908 --> 15:11.994
Never told anyone she had a lover before and deceived us.

252
15:12.620 --> 15:14.872
How do we know there are no other lies?

253
15:14.956 --> 15:17.125
[gasps] Hold your tongue!

254
15:17.750 --> 15:19.293
Do you even hear yourself, girl?

255
15:19.377 --> 15:21.337
Oh, it definitely is his!

256
15:21.420 --> 15:24.048
[sighs deeply] Goodness!

257
15:24.132 --> 15:25.424
[gasps] You!

258
15:25.508 --> 15:27.176
If I hear those words from your mouth again,

259
15:27.260 --> 15:28.678
best believe I'll sew it shut!

260
15:28.761 --> 15:29.762
[groans]

261
15:30.263 --> 15:31.389
[sighs frustratedly]

262
15:31.472 --> 15:33.558
[♪ unsettling music playing]

263
15:35.852 --> 15:37.186
[jewelry clinking]

264
15:38.229 --> 15:39.355
[Lotteshu] Good girl.

265
15:42.150 --> 15:43.276
Your necklace.

266
15:43.359 --> 15:44.861
[scoffs]

267
16:10.678 --> 16:13.681
[Sovieshu humming]

268
16:26.527 --> 16:27.945
[pen scratching]

269
16:29.947 --> 16:32.033
Tell me, is it not delightful?

270
16:32.700 --> 16:34.410
It is a lullaby for my child.

271
16:34.493 --> 16:37.622
[Prime Minister] Most impressive, Your Majesty. Once again, congratulations.

272
16:37.705 --> 16:41.125
-[Minister of Finance] Congratulations. -[ministers] Congratulations.

273
16:45.213 --> 16:46.297
It's lovely.

274
16:47.798 --> 16:50.509
This New Year's Ceremony is a great success.

275
16:51.761 --> 16:52.970
It's all thanks to you.

276
16:54.430 --> 16:58.434
As for the New Year's budget, there are no major changes, but--

277
16:58.517 --> 17:02.772
Any changes will be to Rashta's allowance and for the child.

278
17:04.065 --> 17:06.108
I want you to search for the most skilled midwives

279
17:06.192 --> 17:07.652
in the Eastern Empire.

280
17:08.194 --> 17:09.528
Select about 10.

281
17:21.499 --> 17:23.584
[♪ gentle music playing]

282
17:32.468 --> 17:33.636
[Heinrey] Your Majesty.

283
17:42.979 --> 17:43.980
[chuckles softly]

284
17:45.314 --> 17:46.315
[chuckles]

285
17:47.483 --> 17:48.526
Your Highness!

286
17:49.735 --> 17:51.112
Your steps seem rather hurried.

287
17:51.696 --> 17:52.989
I've had so much to do…

288
17:53.072 --> 17:54.615
and foolishly forgot to eat.

289
17:54.699 --> 17:55.783
I'm hurrying to dinner.

290
17:56.701 --> 17:58.077
What brings you two here?

291
17:58.160 --> 17:59.704
The party. I was invited.

292
18:00.288 --> 18:01.539
The party?

293
18:05.084 --> 18:06.460
My brother's welcome party.

294
18:06.544 --> 18:07.795
It was a secret, was it not?

295
18:07.878 --> 18:09.672
You and Sir Kosair think alike.

296
18:09.755 --> 18:11.674
Although it looks like he got there first.

297
18:12.675 --> 18:14.010
[both chuckling]

298
18:14.093 --> 18:15.344
[chuckles softly]

299
18:16.470 --> 18:18.598
[Kosair laughs] There!

300
18:18.681 --> 18:19.807
Surprised?

301
18:19.890 --> 18:23.102
Today, your dear brother is going to treat everyone who loves you,

302
18:23.185 --> 18:24.937
my wonderful sister.

303
18:25.021 --> 18:26.022
Sit down.

304
18:31.819 --> 18:33.070
Uh…

305
18:36.324 --> 18:39.869
The great ruler who crushed the Springwater Bandits.

306
18:40.369 --> 18:41.954
I truly admire you, sir.

307
18:42.997 --> 18:44.332
This is a gift.

308
18:44.415 --> 18:45.416
I hope you like wine.

309
18:48.210 --> 18:50.254
And who… might you be?

310
18:50.338 --> 18:51.422
Ah…

311
18:51.505 --> 18:52.632
I serve…

312
18:52.715 --> 18:54.550
I serve as First Vanguard and Storm Assault Captain

313
18:54.634 --> 18:57.178
under the Wolf Knights of the Corps of Lions Capital First Defense Command.

314
18:57.261 --> 19:00.306
Also known as the lonely, spotted, and colorful scarlet leopard cat

315
19:00.389 --> 19:01.766
of the Himalayan mountains.

316
19:02.767 --> 19:03.976
I am McKenna.

317
19:04.852 --> 19:05.853
[exclaims excitedly]

318
19:06.896 --> 19:07.938
What Kenna?

319
19:08.439 --> 19:10.274
Uh… McKenna, sir, is what you can call me.

320
19:10.358 --> 19:11.942
Ah, MenKenna.

321
19:12.026 --> 19:13.152
No, Mc…

322
19:13.235 --> 19:14.236
McKenna.

323
19:14.320 --> 19:15.613
-[giggles] -[Kosair] MenKenna.

324
19:15.696 --> 19:16.864
It's Mc.

325
19:17.490 --> 19:18.491
Mc.

326
19:18.574 --> 19:20.201
-Sit down. -Yes.

327
19:22.578 --> 19:26.874
This is a valuable beverage I brought especially for you, my friends.

328
19:26.957 --> 19:30.878
It is a drink designed to hearten the souls of the battlefield.

329
19:31.796 --> 19:33.089
I present this bottle to you,

330
19:33.172 --> 19:36.425
and we'll drink to the happiness of my sister, Empress Navier!

331
19:36.509 --> 19:37.968
-[pops] -[laughing]

332
19:38.052 --> 19:40.805
[guests chuckling and clapping]

333
19:42.181 --> 19:44.433
-[liquid trickling] -I'd wager that this is the first instance

334
19:44.517 --> 19:46.977
Navier has ever called anyone a friend.

335
19:49.980 --> 19:53.484
-Leopard Cat! -Ah, yes! Leopard Cat, McKenna.

336
19:53.567 --> 19:54.610
-Have some. -Thank you, sir.

337
19:54.694 --> 19:56.404
[Navier chuckles]

338
20:00.574 --> 20:02.410
I would like to pour you a drink.

339
20:02.493 --> 20:03.494
[laughs]

340
20:04.620 --> 20:07.289
Now then, to my sister, the Empress.

341
20:07.373 --> 20:08.416
Cheers!

342
20:22.847 --> 20:23.889
[exhales]

343
20:24.765 --> 20:26.976
Oh. [laughs]

344
20:29.562 --> 20:30.563
Oh, oh, oh!

345
20:30.646 --> 20:32.189
Wait a minute. Stop there, wait.

346
20:33.023 --> 20:35.609
This soup is made with very rare mushrooms.

347
20:36.861 --> 20:37.862
Try it.

348
20:38.362 --> 20:39.905
Oh, no, no, no.

349
20:39.989 --> 20:40.990
Ah, eat this too.

350
20:41.073 --> 20:42.658
Eliza, sorry.

351
20:42.742 --> 20:43.951
Oh! Wait, wait, wait.

352
20:44.034 --> 20:45.661
-This too. -It's too much, Kosair!

353
20:45.745 --> 20:47.496
You should know, these are very rare mushrooms

354
20:47.580 --> 20:49.290
which only grow at the border after snowfall.

355
20:49.373 --> 20:53.210
Sir Kosair climbed the cliff himself to forage a few for Your Majesty to try.

356
20:55.588 --> 20:56.881
[exclaiming]

357
20:57.465 --> 20:58.591
[Kosair] This too.

358
20:58.674 --> 21:01.093
-[guests laugh] -You have to eat it all.

359
21:04.638 --> 21:05.681
You…

360
21:07.725 --> 21:08.934
Please forgive me.

361
21:09.018 --> 21:10.853
[chuckling]

362
21:10.936 --> 21:12.646
[Laura] Now, don't push until I tell you.

363
21:12.730 --> 21:13.898
[McKenna] I won't.

364
21:13.981 --> 21:15.399
[Laura] Ready, set…

365
21:16.233 --> 21:17.443
go!

366
21:19.737 --> 21:22.114
What's this? Is this your idea of pushing?

367
21:22.990 --> 21:24.700
That is disappointing, General.

368
21:26.494 --> 21:27.995
Now, I'll count one, two, three.

369
21:28.078 --> 21:30.331
So try pushing. Ready? One, two, three!

370
21:30.414 --> 21:31.415
-Oh! -[cackling]

371
21:31.499 --> 21:33.501
-[all laughing] -But I…

372
21:33.584 --> 21:34.585
-Colorful! -Wait!

373
21:34.668 --> 21:36.420
Scarlet, mm, leopard cat! [laughs]

374
21:36.504 --> 21:39.089
Ah, wait a moment. Just wait one moment. Ah!

375
21:39.173 --> 21:40.549
[groans in pain]

376
21:40.633 --> 21:42.218
-[Kosair] Round two. -[Laura] Sit down once again.

377
21:42.301 --> 21:44.678
-[McKenna] I'll try from the inside out. -Shall we get some air?

378
21:44.762 --> 21:46.722
[Falhan] I'm afraid Sir Kosair is unbeatable!

379
21:51.268 --> 21:52.269
Heinrey…

380
21:53.229 --> 21:55.815
I heard you will return to the Western Kingdom soon.

381
21:58.067 --> 22:00.319
-[sighs deeply] -McKenna mentioned it.

382
22:02.822 --> 22:04.865
Is your brother's illness quite serious?

383
22:07.034 --> 22:09.578
His condition has worsened, I'm afraid.

384
22:09.662 --> 22:11.664
But there's no reason for concern yet.

385
22:13.582 --> 22:15.292
I wanted to ask you a question.

386
22:16.961 --> 22:17.962
Ask away.

387
22:21.799 --> 22:22.925
Your husband…

388
22:24.885 --> 22:25.886
Do you…

389
22:26.762 --> 22:27.972
Do you love him?

390
22:40.359 --> 22:42.361
[♪ poignant music playing]

391
22:52.621 --> 22:54.540
If Sovieshu felt joy…

392
22:57.251 --> 22:59.295
I would also be joyous.

393
23:02.339 --> 23:03.632
We had a bond.

394
23:05.593 --> 23:07.761
Our pains and triumphs were shared.

395
23:13.934 --> 23:15.728
I had thought it would last forever.

396
23:16.228 --> 23:17.313
[sighs softly]

397
23:20.274 --> 23:21.901
That can no longer be.

398
23:49.803 --> 23:52.056
[♪ gentle music playing]

399
24:27.383 --> 24:28.592
[sighs deeply]

400
24:31.053 --> 24:32.179
Why don't you take revenge?

401
24:35.683 --> 24:36.725
Pardon?

402
24:37.643 --> 24:40.896
You could take a very beautiful, high-ranking man as your lover.

403
24:40.980 --> 24:41.981
To show him.

404
24:44.233 --> 24:46.026
I know if you were my lover…

405
24:47.194 --> 24:48.904
Sovieshu may lose his sanity.

406
24:49.655 --> 24:50.823
I didn't say me, did I?

407
24:53.033 --> 24:54.326
[chuckles softly]

408
24:57.329 --> 24:58.539
Your glass is empty.

409
25:01.709 --> 25:03.335
[both chuckle softly]

410
25:03.419 --> 25:04.586
[Navier clears throat]

411
25:05.754 --> 25:06.755
Well, then…

412
25:08.549 --> 25:09.591
Well, what?

413
25:10.676 --> 25:11.885
One…

414
25:11.969 --> 25:14.972
very beautiful, high-ranking, remarkable man.

415
25:16.015 --> 25:17.433
Currently single.

416
25:17.516 --> 25:18.642
[laughs]

417
25:18.726 --> 25:19.727
[chuckles]

418
25:20.853 --> 25:22.521
The ceremony this year…

419
25:24.857 --> 25:26.358
I will never forget it.

420
25:26.442 --> 25:28.819
[♪ music continues playing]

421
25:43.834 --> 25:46.754
[Kosair] Some former Springwater Bandits even sent me a couple of puppies.

422
25:46.837 --> 25:50.424
They were so tiny, I could hold them both in one hand! [exclaims]

423
25:50.507 --> 25:53.260
Navier, I really wish you could have seen them.

424
25:53.343 --> 25:55.637
[both laughing]

425
25:55.721 --> 25:57.347
You are such a sweet man.

426
25:57.973 --> 25:59.683
Why have you found no one yet?

427
26:00.851 --> 26:03.062
Marquess, do you know the reason?

428
26:03.145 --> 26:06.065
Well, Your Majesty, whenever he sees a pretty woman,

429
26:06.148 --> 26:08.984
he becomes so shy that he freezes like a wooden doll.

430
26:09.610 --> 26:10.944
That cannot be true.

431
26:11.028 --> 26:14.990
He breaks into a cold sweat, cannot speak, and his expression is…

432
26:15.074 --> 26:17.367
Hmm. Looks just like that.

433
26:19.203 --> 26:20.204
[shushes]

434
26:21.080 --> 26:23.040
-Who is it? -What do you see?

435
26:30.422 --> 26:32.424
[Falhan] That woman, isn't she…

436
26:33.926 --> 26:35.260
It's Sovieshu's mistress.

437
26:37.387 --> 26:38.472
So, that's her.

438
26:47.481 --> 26:49.108
I was just out taking a stroll.

439
26:49.942 --> 26:53.028
I was told to walk often. The physician recommended it.

440
26:53.904 --> 26:57.950
Our child is already very fussy and is a terribly picky eater.

441
26:58.659 --> 27:01.703
My morning sickness is awful. There's only one thing I can eat.

442
27:01.787 --> 27:03.664
Just apple pie, nothing else.

443
27:03.747 --> 27:06.542
As you know, Your Majesty, apple pie is--

444
27:06.625 --> 27:08.252
It is His Majesty's favorite food.

445
27:08.335 --> 27:09.545
[giggles]

446
27:09.628 --> 27:12.714
Exactly. Imagine when he heard that news…

447
27:12.798 --> 27:13.799
[Navier] All right.

448
27:14.883 --> 27:16.385
Be sure to take care.

449
27:19.138 --> 27:21.014
Rashta's aware you look down on her.

450
27:23.016 --> 27:24.268
Rashta understands.

451
27:25.894 --> 27:28.647
The pregnancy celebration invite was rejected too.

452
27:29.648 --> 27:31.233
Don't be jealous, Your Majesty.

453
27:31.942 --> 27:33.110
It's unbecoming of you.

454
27:36.321 --> 27:37.322
What?

455
27:37.823 --> 27:39.783
You think me less than you.

456
27:39.867 --> 27:42.327
No matter how much your malice shines through,

457
27:42.411 --> 27:43.871
Rashta will keep enduring.

458
27:45.414 --> 27:47.082
I do respect you so.

459
27:47.666 --> 27:48.667
Therefore…

460
27:50.127 --> 27:52.004
I choose not to fight with you any longer.

461
27:52.087 --> 27:53.839
It is for the benefit of my child.

462
27:55.716 --> 27:56.758
Why do you say that?

463
27:57.342 --> 27:59.720
Lady Albani told me all there is to know.

464
27:59.803 --> 28:02.598
How you may, in fact, be infertile

465
28:02.681 --> 28:06.602
and will likely be the adoptive mother of the child that Rashta now carries.

466
28:09.187 --> 28:10.188
What?

467
28:10.939 --> 28:11.940
Girl…

468
28:16.987 --> 28:18.864
Say that again.

469
28:20.282 --> 28:21.867
What are you babbling about?

470
28:23.535 --> 28:25.913
Well, Her Majesty was the one who first…

471
28:28.332 --> 28:29.333
"Adoptive…

472
28:32.085 --> 28:33.545
"mother"?

473
28:35.130 --> 28:36.340
Stop it, brother.

474
28:36.423 --> 28:37.883
[gasps softly]

475
28:37.966 --> 28:39.927
That is my sister.

476
28:40.010 --> 28:41.470
[gasps] I didn't, I…

477
28:41.553 --> 28:43.430
-[Kisia] Oh no, Ms. Rashta! -[Cherini] Are you all right?

478
28:43.513 --> 28:45.098
Why, you little…

479
28:45.182 --> 28:46.683
-Oh no! -Oh no.

480
28:46.767 --> 28:48.101
Sir Kosair, leave her.

481
28:48.185 --> 28:50.187
-You must not get provoked. -[Rashta] The baby!

482
28:50.270 --> 28:51.730
-You… -Ah, my stomach hurts.

483
28:51.813 --> 28:54.775
Say one more word about my Navier being an adoptive mother,

484
28:54.858 --> 28:56.109
or raising your little brat,

485
28:56.193 --> 28:59.321
by my honor, I shall rip the tongue from your lying mouth!

486
28:59.404 --> 29:00.656
[Falhan] Let's go, Kosair!

487
29:01.990 --> 29:03.158
[Cherini] Are you all right?

488
29:03.241 --> 29:06.495
-Your Majesty, please, you must go. -[Kisia] It's going to be all right.

489
29:06.578 --> 29:08.330
[breathing raggedly]

490
29:08.413 --> 29:09.790
-[Kisia] Hurry, hurry. -What happened here?

491
29:09.873 --> 29:11.458
-Over here. The baby! -Are you all right?

492
29:11.541 --> 29:13.168
-What do we do? -You have to help the baby now.

493
29:13.251 --> 29:15.379
[♪ dramatic music playing]

494
29:15.462 --> 29:17.547
-Can you stand? -Oh dear.

495
29:18.131 --> 29:19.800
[moaning]

496
29:40.028 --> 29:41.029
[weakly] Your Majesty.

497
29:43.281 --> 29:44.700
Do not fear, my Rashta.

498
29:45.409 --> 29:46.576
I am here by your side.

499
29:47.369 --> 29:48.745
How is the child doing?

500
29:49.454 --> 29:50.872
Does that matter

501
29:51.581 --> 29:52.666
at a time like this?

502
29:54.459 --> 29:56.628
Rashta cares a lot for the baby.

503
29:58.338 --> 30:01.216
I think that you are far more important.

504
30:02.592 --> 30:03.802
Oh.

505
30:06.346 --> 30:07.347
A damp cloth.

506
30:18.025 --> 30:19.860
I'd like to talk with you outside.

507
30:26.283 --> 30:27.284
How is she?

508
30:27.367 --> 30:29.953
She needs rest until she has recovered.

509
30:30.579 --> 30:31.913
Is it anything serious?

510
30:31.997 --> 30:34.499
[physician] In the early stages of pregnancy, one must be careful.

511
30:34.583 --> 30:36.793
Ms. Rashta was never strong to begin with.

512
30:37.335 --> 30:40.047
If she is not careful, then she could suffer a miscarriage.

513
30:40.130 --> 30:41.715
So this cannot happen again.

514
30:43.341 --> 30:45.302
[exhales heavily]

515
30:47.387 --> 30:49.014
[sighs furiously]

516
30:51.016 --> 30:52.225
[grunts]

517
30:54.102 --> 30:55.729
[vase clanking]

518
30:57.898 --> 30:59.524
[breathing shakily]

519
30:59.608 --> 31:00.609
[exhales]

520
31:12.579 --> 31:14.498
The physician said not to worry about anything.

521
31:18.335 --> 31:20.253
Would you hold my hand?

522
31:28.386 --> 31:30.013
I heard you went to the garden…

523
31:30.972 --> 31:33.141
and saw the Empress and General Kosair.

524
31:36.269 --> 31:37.354
[exhales shakily]

525
31:37.437 --> 31:39.606
He screamed as if he wanted to kill me.

526
31:40.357 --> 31:42.984
I fell after he pushed me.

527
31:43.068 --> 31:44.653
He was intimidating and threatening.

528
31:44.736 --> 31:45.862
It was scary.

529
31:47.823 --> 31:48.824
Pushed you?

530
31:54.162 --> 31:55.163
Is that true?

531
31:57.165 --> 31:59.000
-It is, yes. -[gasps] Hmm?

532
32:00.043 --> 32:01.294
[whispers] What…

533
32:02.087 --> 32:04.589
-What… -You must tell His Majesty the truth.

534
32:13.765 --> 32:16.101
Yes, it's true, Your Majesty.

535
32:16.184 --> 32:17.644
[sighs]

536
32:23.316 --> 32:25.068
The child is what angered him.

537
32:26.069 --> 32:28.947
He does not want Rashta to have Your Majesty's baby.

538
32:29.030 --> 32:30.031
[breathes shakily]

539
32:31.158 --> 32:33.118
The Empress looked at me with such…

540
32:33.201 --> 32:34.661
cold eyes.

541
32:34.744 --> 32:36.079
It was frightening.

542
32:36.163 --> 32:37.914
She felt the same as her brother.

543
32:40.375 --> 32:41.918
And that is the truth.

544
32:46.965 --> 32:48.550
[♪ foreboding music playing]

545
33:15.660 --> 33:17.370
Kosair is banished from the palace?

546
33:17.454 --> 33:19.414
They say it is His Majesty's order.

547
33:19.998 --> 33:23.710
"As an investigation has begun into the assault against Ms. Rashta,

548
33:23.793 --> 33:25.921
"Sir Kosair is to leave the palace."

549
33:26.004 --> 33:27.005
[gasps]

550
33:27.088 --> 33:28.965
"He is to wait outside the palace walls

551
33:29.716 --> 33:31.968
"until his punishment is decided."

552
33:32.052 --> 33:34.888
[groans] Sovieshu, that son of a bitch.

553
33:34.971 --> 33:36.223
The order makes no sense.

554
33:36.932 --> 33:40.018
I'll march out there and butcher every soldier in my way

555
33:40.101 --> 33:42.145
just to explain it to that bastard.

556
33:42.229 --> 33:44.439
-[Eliza] Please restrain yourself, sir. -General!

557
33:44.981 --> 33:47.067
-Step aside. -Should you choose to fight…

558
33:47.734 --> 33:49.277
I will stand beside you as always.

559
33:49.361 --> 33:52.072
But it puts Her Majesty into a complicated situation.

560
33:56.451 --> 33:57.452
[Kosair groans angrily]

561
34:02.374 --> 34:04.042
Arrest him.

562
34:04.125 --> 34:05.627
Just try.

563
34:18.223 --> 34:19.641
[groans angrily]

564
34:20.684 --> 34:22.227
They claimed it was assault?

565
34:22.811 --> 34:25.730
They say that the general pushed Rashta, Your Majesty.

566
34:27.065 --> 34:28.066
[sighs in disbelief]

567
34:41.788 --> 34:42.789
[door closes]

568
34:43.748 --> 34:44.749
[exhales]

569
34:45.625 --> 34:46.668
It is Rashta.

570
34:47.502 --> 34:48.837
She claims she was pushed.

571
34:49.379 --> 34:51.172
My brother did not touch her.

572
34:51.256 --> 34:52.424
[exhales]

573
34:52.507 --> 34:53.842
She is mistaken.

574
34:54.592 --> 34:55.927
I witnessed it all.

575
34:56.845 --> 34:58.388
Her report is not true.

576
34:58.471 --> 34:59.848
And my brother is innocent.

577
35:00.432 --> 35:01.891
[sighs]

578
35:01.975 --> 35:03.435
You expect me to believe that?

579
35:03.518 --> 35:07.063
I have always been honest with you. Do you believe I would lie, Your Majesty?

580
35:07.147 --> 35:09.232
It is already decided.

581
35:09.316 --> 35:12.110
Kosair was seen pushing her by witnesses.

582
35:13.903 --> 35:15.780
Your Majesty has lost his eyes and ears.

583
35:15.864 --> 35:18.116
I nearly lost my child!

584
35:18.700 --> 35:21.077
It is not important if Rashta lied or not.

585
35:21.161 --> 35:22.746
The problem is you.

586
35:22.829 --> 35:26.499
You refuse to accept and acknowledge that I am having a baby.

587
35:27.500 --> 35:28.918
Your cold animosity…

588
35:29.628 --> 35:32.756
it reveals a blatant truth within your being.

589
35:32.839 --> 35:35.508
Kosair was moved to act this way because of you.

590
35:38.178 --> 35:39.679
And you should know that…

591
35:40.263 --> 35:43.558
this decision is my consideration for you.

592
35:47.771 --> 35:49.397
How very charitable of you.

593
35:52.025 --> 35:53.485
This is a warning.

594
35:54.194 --> 35:56.279
You will cease your hostility at once.

595
35:57.197 --> 35:59.908
If anything like this happens to my child again, then I will not…

596
36:01.493 --> 36:02.869
forgive Kosair.

597
36:05.538 --> 36:07.123
And I will not forgive you.

598
36:08.708 --> 36:10.710
[♪ tense music playing]

599
36:38.988 --> 36:42.701
[Rashta] You clearly saw the Empress' older brother push me, didn't you?

600
36:42.784 --> 36:44.536
Listen, you must tell the truth!

601
36:44.619 --> 36:46.121
[hesitatingly] I don't know.

602
36:46.204 --> 36:47.497
I don't think I saw anything.

603
36:47.580 --> 36:48.623
He pushed Rashta!

604
36:48.707 --> 36:49.708
He absolutely did.

605
36:49.791 --> 36:51.751
He pushed Rashta. He pushed me, and you saw.

606
36:51.835 --> 36:54.713
-And that is the truth. Do you understand? -Yes, I understand, Ms. Rashta.

607
36:54.796 --> 36:56.548
-[door opens] -[Kisia] Ms. Rashta!

608
36:57.173 --> 37:00.343
Her Majesty's older brother has been ordered out the palace.

609
37:00.427 --> 37:02.178
The knights seized him and dragged him away.

610
37:02.262 --> 37:04.931
And they say that His Majesty scolded the Empress,

611
37:05.014 --> 37:07.308
and she was driven out in tears.

612
37:07.392 --> 37:08.476
Really?

613
37:09.644 --> 37:11.020
[exhales]

614
37:12.147 --> 37:13.148
[sighs in relief]

615
37:14.107 --> 37:15.275
[door closes]

616
37:15.942 --> 37:16.943
Your Highness,

617
37:17.485 --> 37:18.737
where are you going?

618
37:19.237 --> 37:20.905
Sir Kosair was chased out of the palace.

619
37:20.989 --> 37:22.073
Your Highness…

620
37:27.746 --> 37:29.581
A letter has arrived from our homeland.

621
37:33.084 --> 37:34.961
[♪ somber music playing]

622
37:39.549 --> 37:42.218
HIS MAJESTY KING WALTON III IS IN CRITICAL CONDITION

623
37:44.471 --> 37:45.472
I should…

624
37:46.931 --> 37:47.974
return now.

625
37:49.309 --> 37:50.727
That decision is wise.

626
37:51.311 --> 37:52.937
Your ascension is guaranteed.

627
37:53.021 --> 37:56.441
And the next successor after you is far removed.

628
37:56.524 --> 37:59.736
But it would still be best for you to return quickly.

629
38:01.571 --> 38:02.697
To hear the final words.

630
38:10.455 --> 38:12.123
-[door opens] -[sighs heavily]

631
38:12.624 --> 38:13.625
[door closes]

632
38:20.507 --> 38:22.509
[♪ wistful music playing]

633
38:52.789 --> 38:53.832
Here you are.

634
38:53.915 --> 38:55.250
I've been looking for you.

635
38:56.209 --> 38:57.377
What do you need?

636
38:57.460 --> 39:00.713
Marquess Lante has news from the Western Kingdom, Your Majesty.

637
39:01.297 --> 39:03.633
Their king is said to be critically ill.

638
39:06.761 --> 39:08.137
His kingdom needs him.

639
39:09.055 --> 39:10.431
Prince Heinrey must return.

640
39:10.515 --> 39:11.933
I'm afraid he must.

641
39:12.016 --> 39:14.978
His delegation will leave tonight, Your Majesty.

642
39:15.645 --> 39:17.313
Since invitees fall under your jurisdiction--

643
39:17.397 --> 39:18.773
As soon as possible?

644
39:20.441 --> 39:21.568
Yes.

645
39:25.363 --> 39:26.948
Will you bid him farewell?

646
39:36.291 --> 39:37.333
I think not.

647
39:39.878 --> 39:41.629
It is not wise to do so.

648
39:44.424 --> 39:47.385
Lady Eliza, do everything in your power

649
39:47.468 --> 39:49.095
to ensure his safe return.

650
39:49.178 --> 39:52.140
Yes. I will, Your Majesty.

651
40:04.068 --> 40:05.069
[sighs]

652
40:12.243 --> 40:13.244
[chirps softly]

653
40:15.496 --> 40:17.498
[♪ gentle music playing]

654
40:34.891 --> 40:39.020
It is my honor to meet you, my queen.

655
40:40.021 --> 40:42.774
Are you a good dancer, Your Majesty?

656
40:47.195 --> 40:49.739
[Navier] If you are sharing your thoughts through these letters,

657
40:49.822 --> 40:51.157
why meet at all?

658
40:51.240 --> 40:54.911
They are too special. I must meet that person.

659
40:55.745 --> 40:57.914
Your Majesty, I'm so glad it was you.

660
40:59.290 --> 41:00.500
I really mean it.

661
41:02.251 --> 41:04.545
[Navier] I was so thrilled that it was you.

662
41:07.674 --> 41:09.342
I'm so grateful.

663
41:26.484 --> 41:30.113
Prince Heinrey, your friendship has healed many wounds

664
41:30.196 --> 41:32.365
I would not have been able to treat alone.

665
41:35.535 --> 41:37.537
You are a truly good person.

666
41:39.163 --> 41:41.165
[♪ music continues playing]

667
41:41.249 --> 41:42.625
[sighs heavily]

668
41:44.836 --> 41:47.714
[Heinrey] I did not know our parting would come so soon.

669
41:53.970 --> 41:56.973
[Navier] I wonder how many more opportunities there will be

670
41:57.056 --> 41:59.517
for us to meet in this lifetime.

671
42:07.567 --> 42:10.153
Goodbye, Heinrey.

672
42:21.748 --> 42:22.749
[♪ music fades]

673
42:30.298 --> 42:31.966
[Albani] They say that if a man eats this,

674
42:33.301 --> 42:34.927
his seed will dry up.

675
42:35.428 --> 42:38.139
For a woman, her field will be unfruitful.

676
42:38.723 --> 42:41.601
She'd be infertile for the rest of her life.

677
42:41.684 --> 42:43.686
[♪ ominous music playing]

678
42:52.028 --> 42:53.279
Keep this secret…

679
42:54.113 --> 42:55.990
until it is all over.

680
42:57.158 --> 42:58.576
With the stars as our witness,

681
42:59.494 --> 43:01.913
your secret will be safe here.

682
43:01.996 --> 43:04.165
Only the two of us will know, Your Majesty.

683
43:04.248 --> 43:05.374
[door opens]

684
43:05.458 --> 43:09.045
Your Highness, Lady Navier, please don't run.

685
43:10.004 --> 43:11.506
[chuckling]

686
43:12.673 --> 43:14.217
That dear child…

687
43:17.095 --> 43:18.679
is destined to lead us.

688
43:19.680 --> 43:21.724
Soon, all the Mistresses will arrive.

689
43:21.808 --> 43:24.352
[Albani] I will have them prepared with tea.

690
43:25.686 --> 43:28.064
I have faith those wenches will enjoy them.

691
43:28.147 --> 43:30.191
[Albani] Do not worry, Your Majesty.

692
43:47.792 --> 43:49.794
[♪ music continues playing]

693
44:21.993 --> 44:27.415
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

694
44:27.498 --> 44:29.500
[♪ closing theme music playing]
